browser-harness-js SDK (skills/cdp/sdk), vendored because it is not published to npm.

Upstream: https://github.com/monotykamary/browser-harness-js
Commit:   3c436dcbed8a597cfc2e338c47eaccf9b643a31b (2026-10-30, SDK 0.19.0)
License:  MIT (LICENSE in this directory)

Files: browser.ts chrome.ts extension-hub.ts generated.ts interaction.ts page.ts
       session.ts snapshot.ts wire.ts ws-server.ts
Fork-only: navigation-state.ts (Page.goto settles on the requested document's DOMContentLoaded, not load).
Not vendored: recording.ts (the rrweb DOM tape), tests, gen.ts, repl.ts, the protocol JSON.

Historical vendor baseline: the guard patches this directory used to carry (transparent native controls, the sensitive-field
grant, readable-frame limits, role locators on large pages, refusal reasons) are upstream since 20fc83d. Since
3c436dc upstream also carries the flow-runner pilot's last patches: trusted fill types like a person (click,
select-all, a key per keyable character, other scripts committed whole, long text pasted), native date and time
controls, maskSensitive, transparent file inputs, closed-shadow host hits and headers on connect. typeKeys and
SELECT_ALL_MODIFIER are exported from interaction.ts, so @midscene/web/browser-harness re-exports them from here
(the browser-harness/keys.ts copy is gone).

Keep this directory out of the formatter and linter (biome.json files.ignore) so it stays byte-comparable with
upstream.

Fork-local changes past that baseline: ScopeBinding carries the authored targetRole/targetName/targetExact and
Page.perform refuses a resolved node that is no longer that target (scope_target_mismatch) before dispatch; refusal
descriptions withhold sensitive and masked text under the grant; goto waits for document readiness. A blocked action
reports the guard's own refusal before the DOM diagnostic; raw commit values reach the host only for a declared
secret; private-marked scroll regions are offered under the sensitive grant like other private-marked controls.
A field is sensitive by its type, autocomplete or private mark only; the name list is gone, so an ordinary named
field (username, first name, postal code) keeps a readable value under maskSensitive.
